  "description": "Backend-observed latency for synthetic log probes sent through the normal OpenTelemetry pipeline.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "### What this measures\n\nThe load generator emits an OpenTelemetry Event named `demo.telemetry.pipeline.probe` and exports it immediately. The probe follows the normal log path through the Collector, exporter batching, network, and OpenSearch. At ingest, OpenSearch subtracts the LogRecord `Timestamp` from its own ingest time.\n\nThis is **backend-observed latency for the probe path**, not a per-node breakdown. It requires synchronized producer and backend clocks. Missing probes indicate an availability problem; negative samples are reported separately as possible clock skew.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.5.2",
      "title": "Backend-observed telemetry pipeline latency",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
      "description": "At least one probe should arrive during every two-minute window. A zero value means the probe path is unavailable or the emitter is stopped.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "No probes received",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 5 },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.5.2",
      "targets": [
        {
          "bucketAggs": [],
          "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
          "format": "table",
          "metrics": [ { "id": "1", "type": "count" } ],
          "query": "eventName.keyword:\"demo.telemetry.pipeline.probe\" AND probe_received_at:[now-2m TO now]",
          "queryType": "lucene",
          "refId": "A",
          "timeField": "probe_received_at"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Probes received (last 2m)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
      "description": "Negative latency indicates that the producer clock is ahead of the OpenSearch clock. These samples are excluded from latency aggregates.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "0",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 1 }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 5 },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.5.2",
      "targets": [
        {
          "bucketAggs": [],
          "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
          "format": "table",
          "metrics": [ { "id": "1", "type": "count" } ],
          "query": "eventName.keyword:\"demo.telemetry.pipeline.probe\" AND probe_clock_skew_detected:true",
          "queryType": "lucene",
          "refId": "A",
          "timeField": "probe_received_at"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Clock-skew samples",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
      "description": "Number of successfully received probes in the selected time range. Use this to judge whether tail percentiles have enough samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [ { "color": "blue", "value": null } ] },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 5 },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.5.2",
      "targets": [
        {
          "bucketAggs": [],
          "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
          "format": "table",
          "metrics": [ { "id": "1", "type": "count" } ],
          "query": "eventName.keyword:\"demo.telemetry.pipeline.probe\"",
          "queryType": "lucene",
          "refId": "A",
          "timeField": "probe_received_at"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Probe samples",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": { "type": "grafana-opensearch-datasource", "uid": "webstore-logs" },
      "description": "Time from probe emission to OpenSearch ingest. Tail latency commonly exposes exporter batching and backpressure that averages hide.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "palette-classic" },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": { "legend": false, "tooltip": false, "viz": false },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": { "type": "linear" },
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": { "group": "A", "mode": "none" },
            "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "off" }
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [ { "color": "green", "value": null } ] },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 12, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 10 },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
